through 21 chapters of patient accounting and hits with corresponding force.\n\nThe weaknesses are real. The middle section drags. The relay structure Ilinca uses to trace transmission branches — bread-queue acquaintance reaches pharmacy contact, delivery boy carries a folded note — is inventive and credible, but by Chapter 16 it has been executed three times and the reader understands the mechanism before Ilinca deploys it again. Munteanu is also the thinnest narrator: his procedural chapters are gripping but he is less emotionally present on the page.\n\nBut the final third recovers everything. The convergence — Ilinca's decision, Munteanu working toward the same address, the December 5 deadline — is handled with the precision that characterizes the novel's best work. The ending, Doina on the Somes bank reciting the document to the fog and getting the bracket right, closes the formal argument and the emotional arc at the same moment.\n\nThis is a book a smart general reader will keep reading and finish glad they did. You would not be annoyed you bought it."
